  "verdict_text": "On this CAS-labeled English corpus (n=457), a linear probe on Pythia-160M layer-3 hidden states recovers the noetic label at test accuracy 0.899 (macro-F1 0.902), against a 10% chance baseline. A TF-IDF + logistic-regression baseline on the same text reaches 0.884; the Pythia probe adds +1.4 pp over text alone. A shuffled-label control on the same layer drops to 0.101, ruling out a split leak. This evidence is consistent with Pythia's internal representations carrying noetic-axis information beyond what is recoverable from surface wording, but the marginal lift over the TF-IDF baseline is modest. Causal-influence (ablation) and paraphrase-control tests are required before any claim that Pythia mechanistically encodes CAS structure beyond lexical association. Verdict treated as tamper-evident, reproducible, independently inspectable; not as proof of mechanistic alignment.",
